; Frama-C EVA benchmark: a standalone executable that statically links
; the Frama-C kernel + the EVA (value/abstract-interpretation) plugin.
;
; This mirrors Frama-C's own `frama-c` binary (upstream's empty_file
; exe): an empty main module whose behaviour comes entirely from the
; link-time registration side-effects of the linked libraries.  -linkall
; forces every module (incl. EVA's Plugin.Register) to be linked.
;
; CRUX: frama-c-eva.core MUST come before frama-c.boot in (libraries).
; boot's module-init finalises the kernel command-line option table, so
; EVA's registration must run first — otherwise `-eva` is unknown.
;
; Run with `-no-autoload-plugins` (see frama-c.build.sh wrapper): EVA is
; statically registered, so the dune-site plugin loader is never invoked
; and no plugin site / .cmxs is needed — the limitation that originally
; parked Frama-C does not apply to this static-link build.
(executable
 (name frama_c_eva)
 (modes exe)
 (flags (:standard -open Frama_c_kernel -linkall))
 (libraries frama-c.kernel frama-c.init.cmdline frama-c-eva.core frama-c.boot))
